    board(pm): file CF-180 — a board-only commit absorbs a sibling lane's event line
    
    Third write for tick code-factory-duckbrain-pm-2026-11-04-07-36-30. The tick's PM
    work already landed (cb62578 filed CF-175, c7ff2bf recorded the DuckBrain receipt),
    so this pass verified those claims against the published tree and filed one row for
    a defect the close-out could not name: this lane's own audit event (285, task
    CF-099) was swept into the sibling dogfood lane's commit 50b4ba3 ("append third-pass
    verification event for CF-179 (event 284)"), whose message and ch:trace never mention
    it. `git show --stat 50b4ba3` = 1 file, 2 insertions; `git log -1 --format=%B 50b4ba3
    | grep -c '285\|CF-099'` = 0. events.jsonl is one shared append-only file, boardctl
    serializes the write but nothing binds a commit's message to the lines it picks up,
    and docs/BOARD.md's write rules say nothing about it.
    
    CF-180 (P4, complexity 2) carries a 289-char probed command and four acceptance
    criteria: reproduce on 50b4ba3, state the write rule in docs/BOARD.md, ship a
    re-runnable recipe that flags event ids a commit adds but does not name, and prove it
    with a selftest arm that is RED before the rule and GREEN after.
    
    Verified before filing, at published tip 1fea92d: CF-175 present with a 464-char
    probe; docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md:5 anchor bc68e59 reproduces (148 rows / 273 events /
    35 sections); docs/audits/cf099-prd-drift-probe.sh -> OK rc 0 with 14 open blockers;
    tests/selftest.sh -> SELFTEST: PASS rc 0; gitreins CF-099-PM1104 PASS at
    .gitreins/history/2026-11-04/03fe5d4d bound to cb62578; board sha256 equal to the
    origin/main blobs and parity 0/0 before this pass wrote anything; writer census
    CENSUS_EMPTY=1. `gh run list --repo coding-hermes/code-factory` = [] (no workflows;
    selftest plus the GitReins guard are the gate of record).
    
    DuckBrain addendum cf0f498f-e23d-458f-b459-a75e2ba71331 was appended to the tick key
    /code-factory/ticks/code-factory-duckbrain-pm-2026-11-04-07-36-30 superseding
    7ae5d165-7f38-43e3-865c-659a5dbab2c4 (readback: POST 201, GET 200, content
    byte-identical, 3184 chars; domain raw_note, namespace code-factory).
    
    Landed from a fresh clone at 4abc422: the registered checkout was two commits behind
    origin/main and carried the sibling lane's in-flight edits (scripts/lib.sh,
    scripts/node-create.sh, scripts/verify-node.sh, tests/selftest.sh), so its board was
    stale. This lane's two board lines were detached from that tree before the clone
    write, so they could not be swept into another lane's commit a second time. The
    shared checkout was left otherwise untouched; its uncommitted paths belong to the
    dogfood lane. The clone installs no hooks, so the GitReins guard is not silently
    skipped by a hook — it is simply not invoked on this board-only commit.
    
